 # False Positive Check
 
+## Toolchain integration
+
+Read [AGENTS.md](../../../AGENTS.md) before applying the upstream workflow below.
+Bash, Write, and Edit are removed from `allowed-tools`. Commands and file writes then follow the normal permission rules of the host.
+The plugin agents that deep verification names are not installed. Do those phases in the current session, or with a general subagent if the host has one.
+Prefer pseudocode PoCs. Create an executable or unit test PoC only in an isolated temporary directory with synthetic data.
+Do not run a PoC against real repositories, user data, remote services, or the network.
+Do not add a PoC or regression test to the repository unless the user asks for that change.
+The verdict is evidence for a human decision. It does not accept, ignore, or postpone a security risk.
+Write the report in Russian.
+
+## Upstream workflow
+
 ## When to Use
 
 - "Is this bug real?" or "is this a true positive?"
